    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 3.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="234" ed="#liebermann"/>Si tunc hominem inuenire non possit cui dederit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#IVAtr_3-2.lnote.oe.31"/>, reddat ipsum tolneum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#IVAtr_3-2.lnote.oe.32"/> et persoluat, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#IVAtr_3-2.lnote.oe.33"/> quinque libras regi.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="74" ed="#robertson"/>Si tunc hominem invenire non possit cui dederit<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_3-2.robnote.fn.1"/>, reddat ipsum tolneum et persolvat et<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_3-2.robnote.fn.2"/> quinque libras regi.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="235" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er aber den Mann, dem er [ihn] gezahlt hat, nicht finden kann, so gebe er den Zoll und zahle ihn nochmals<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_3-2.lnote.de.1"/>, und 5 Pfund<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_3-2.lnote.de.2"/> dem König.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he cannot find the man to whom he paid [it], let him give the toll and pay it again, and 5 pounds to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="75" ed="#robertson"/>If, however, he cannot produce the man to whom he paid it, he shall pay the actual toll and as much again<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_3-2.robnote.n.1"/> and 5 pounds to the king<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_3-2.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dedit <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dedit Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">telon. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">telon. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Wb: persolvere</hi> 2. Orig. las <hi rend="italic">agifan</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">forgieldan</hi>. Die Busse (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 136) erhält der Vogt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Wb: persolvere</hi> 2. The orig. read <hi rend="italic">agifan</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">forgieldan</hi>. The compensation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 136) goes to the reeve</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Königsschutz’; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5. 8; <hi rend="italic">vgl. u</hi>. 4, 1³. Also strenger als im parallelen Falle des durch Anefang (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 16ff.) Beklagten, dem der Gewährsmann fehlt und doch nur einfacher Verlust des Eingeklagten droht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘King's protection’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5. 8; <hi rend="italic">cf. below</hi> 4, 1³. Thus stricter than in the parallel case of a man sued by attachment (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 16ff.) who lacks a warrantor, and who nevertheless risks only the simple loss of the thing claimed</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Probably A.S. <hi rend="italic">forgieldan</hi>. Only one of the five MSS of Q has <hi rend="italic">et</hi>, but cf. In. 9; 31. Liebermann takes it in this way.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. 4, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>dederit</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">dedit</hi> Br.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_3-2.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>et</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">R; om. T, M, Hk, Br.</seg></note>
      </div>
